1079	## Technical names stay
1080	
1081	STE-100 keeps technical names, and a security report cannot work without them:
1082	`reentrancy`, `slippage`, `oracle`, `revert`, `overflow`, `rounding`, `allowance`, `nonce`,
1083	`slot`, `delegatecall`. Use them. They are precise and the reader who fixes Solidity knows
1084	them.
1085	
1086	The rule is what goes **around** them: name the mechanism once with its technical name, then
1087	say in plain words what the attacker gets.
1088	
1089	- No: `Classic CEI violation enabling reentrant drainage of the vault.`
1090	- Yes: `The function sends ETH before it lowers the balance, so a reentrant call withdraws
1091	  the same deposit twice.`
1092	
