1092	## Technical names stay
1093	
1094	STE-100 keeps technical names, and a security report cannot work without them:
1095	`reentrancy`, `slippage`, `oracle`, `revert`, `overflow`, `rounding`, `allowance`, `nonce`,
1096	`slot`, `delegatecall`. Use them. They are precise and the reader who fixes Solidity knows
1097	them.
1098	
1099	The rule is what goes **around** them: name the mechanism once with its technical name, then
1100	say in plain words what the attacker gets.
1101	
1102	- No: `Classic CEI violation enabling reentrant drainage of the vault.`
1103	- Yes: `The function sends ETH before it lowers the balance, so a reentrant call withdraws
1104	  the same deposit twice.`
